                <pb facs="0599" n="583" sameAs="frus:frus1951v01/pg583"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi>
                </head>
                <p>On the evening of November 7, 1951, President Truman delivered a radio and
                    television report to the American people on international arms reduction, with
                    particular reference to the United States United Kingdom-France declaration
                    released in Paris earlier in the day. For text of the tripartite declaration,
                    see telegram Delga 72, <hi rendition="#italic">supra</hi>. For text of the
                    President’s address, see <hi rendition="#italic">Public Papers of the Presidents
                        of the United States: Harry S. Truman, 1951</hi>, pages 623–627, or
                    Department of State <hi rendition="#italic">Bulletin</hi>, November 19, 1951,
                    pages 799–803.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
